    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Hello @aymeric-giraudet I can't understand the logic of this expression. Could you help me. I checked `warn` description:\n\n`Logs a warning if the condition is not met.` \n\nhttps://github.com/algolia/instantsearch/blob/c133170e563592dfc15a95daced1f8447327a09a/packages/react-instantsearch-core/src/lib/warn.ts#L11-L15\n\nOriginally I expected to skip warning by setting `ignoreMultipleHooksWarning` to `true`, but it does not work because when first condition is false the second condition never executed. I could expect: `countRef.current <= parentIndex.getWidgets().length || ignoreMultipleHooksWarning` in this case.\n\nCould you check it please? I could prepare PR if needed. I checked example in repository https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch/tree/b4cb69c8cfaa9dc22dfe8fe695568cf5200f3893/examples/react/next-app-router and in dev it shows the error when it's not expected.",
    "commit_id": "1cf27fdd87232760f2f6f5b9254e78d63852a0cb",
    "created_at": "2025-11-25T18:58:08Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -89,22 +93,32 @@ export function useWidget<TWidget extends Widget | IndexWidget, TProps>({\n \n   if (\n     shouldAddWidgetEarly ||\n-    waitingForResultsRef?.current?.status === 'pending'\n+    waitForResultsRef?.current?.status === 'pending'\n   ) {\n     parentIndex.addWidgets([widget]);\n   }\n \n-  if (\n-    typeof window === 'undefined' &&\n-    waitingForResultsRef?.current &&\n-    // We need the widgets contained in the index to be added before we trigger the search request.\n-    widget.$$type !== 'ais.index'\n-  ) {\n-    use(waitingForResultsRef.current);\n+  if (waitForResultsRef?.current && !skipSuspense) {\n+    use(waitForResultsRef.current);\n     // If we made a second request because of DynamicWidgets, we need to wait for the second result,\n     // except for DynamicWidgets itself which needs to render its children after the first result.\n     if (widget.$$type !== 'ais.dynamicWidgets' && search.helper?.lastResults) {\n-      use(waitingForResultsRef.current);\n+      use(waitForResultsRef.current);\n     }\n   }\n+\n+  if (waitForResultsRef?.current?.status === 'fulfilled') {\n+    countRef.current += 1;\n+    warn(\n+      countRef.current > parentIndex.getWidgets().length &&\n+        !ignoreMultipleHooksWarning,",
